From faa0fdd6b322f4e6abf7918ba1130af0434f3926 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Gaspar <andrew.gaspar@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 06:48:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Menu search: tolerate dictated punctuation and filler words
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The menu's search field is where dictation lands, and a speech model emits a
sentence: "Open Spotify." rather than "spotify". Every term had to be a
substring of the row's name text, so the trailing period and the word "open"
each defeated a query that was otherwise a perfect hit — "Chrome.", "Music.",
"Terminal." and "Open the browser." all found nothing.

Fold both sides of the comparison instead. normalizeSearchText extends the
`._-` fold searchableToken already applied to ids and aliases across labels,
descriptions and the query; searchTerms drops the words a spoken sentence puts
around a name, and falls back to the literal query when that would leave
nothing, so "." and "the" still filter rather than listing every row. A term
the substring pass rejects gets one more chance as a word-anchored subsequence
of the label, which catches "gogle chrome" and "nodejs" and scores in a new
tier below every literal hit.

Two stock bugs surfaced on the way, both fixed here:

- An app row's id is "apps." plus the whole desktop-file stem, so taking its
  leaf handed search a vendor-stripped fragment (org.gnome.Nautilus searched
  as "Nautilus") or the literal word "desktop" (org.telegram.desktop). App
  rows carry the stem as appId; use it, and leave leafIdFor to the menu ids it
  was written for.
- The label went into the name text unfolded while everything around it was
  folded, so "nodejs" missed Node.js and "xournal" missed Xournal++.

The normalizer runs on the query, never on filterText: the search field still
shows the sentence that was said, and dmenu still returns it verbatim.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017qqAVUizVkijbGHd3xnFMw
